"P1399071858" "Bring in Sergeant Fieldman"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4067018625" "You defeated Sergeant Fieldman!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1090146216" "You've brought in Sergeant Fieldman, but the Sky Raiders have taken Zanella!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1399490022" "This is worse than I thought, {HeroName}. I never would've dreamed that the Malta group would be behind this, but it all makes sense. Are you familiar with them? They're a shadow organization that is out to kill all supers, afraid that they're going to take over the world. Sort of like a certain alternate dimension that we're all aware of. It sounds as if they were using Fieldman and Harken to get their hands on the medi-port technology with help from the Sky Raiders. We're lucky, though, that they're using Sky Raiders; it means that Malta is trying to have as minimal a presence in this operation as possible. This man called 'Peter' is probably the Malta liason between the Rogue PPD and Sky Raiders.<br><br>We could discuss the motives and twists of Malta for days on end, but we have a deadline to meet. The Sky Raiders want us to deliver the medi-port tech to them in exchange for Zanella's life. Unfortunately, Medi-Corp hasn't finished making duplicates of the medi-port tech. I don't know what's taking them so long, but I've filed my complaints with the FBSA. This means that we only have the original copy of the tech to exchange. We have no choice but to give the Sky Raiders the medi-port tech."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Nance 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2401314588" "{HeroName}. I've been briefed by Roy Cooling about the current situation. It's a bit ironic that we're handling a conspiracy with people having medi-porters when your double died because {Hero.gender=male he|she} didn't have one, don't you think?"
// Answer Text :
"P545009155" "... Look, will you help me on this operation?"
// Answer Text :
"P1503764726" "... You know, on second thought, I don't need your help."
// Page HelpMe Text :
"P1044603234" "I will. I'll make my way to the base now. There should be a computer terminal in there somewhere. When the coast is clear, message me on the terminal and I'll meet you."
// Answer Text :
"P1139723102" "Sounds good."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - NanceDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3285583505" "<color orange>You enter in a message on the computer to contact Keith Nance.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Roy 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page ArrestedLeader Text :
"P2469609645" "Kiddo, it's been a wild trip, hasn't it? We've got this Peter fellow in custody now. Harken is telling us that he never met this fellow before in his life, and I'm inclined to believe him. We got off lucky today with Malta, let me tell you. I'd hate to have seen what would've happened if they made off with that medi-porter technology.<br><br>Speaking of which, there's been some interesting developments on that side. Zanella and Medi-Corp have come to a new conclusion after all the events that've gone down. While they can't make medi-porters available to <i>every</i> citizen, Medi-Corp is starting a program where they'll give out medi-porters to the handicapped and elderly of Paragon City. Their reasoning is that these are the people who need them the most, given that if they're in a life threatening situation, these folks won't be able to get themselves to a hospital. While the folks who were pushing for the widespread handout of the tech still aren't fully happy, they've at least got something.<br><br>Finally, the boys at Medi-Corp have finished implementing the new tech. About time, huh? You would think they'd need it to get lost a few more times before gettin' it right. This means you hero folks are gonna be a-OK when you're going up against Cole's big bad Praetorians. As for me? Well, I've still got some business here on behalf of the FBSA, like dealing with Lawrence Harken's arrest. Shame about Harken, but that's what happens when good men are blinded by their own ambitions.<br><br>Anyway, I'm sure you've got plenty of other issues to handle, and I've got a wife who is gonna kill me if I don't make it home for dinner at least once this week."
// Answer Text :
"P790492887" "See you around, Roy."
// Page EscapedLeader Text :
"P2979792283" "Kiddo, it's been a wild trip, hasn't it? We've got this Peter fellow in custody now. We got off lucky today with Malta, let me tell you. I'd hate to have seen what would've happened if they made off with that medi-porter technology.<br><br>Speaking of which, there's been some interesting developments on that side. Zanella and Medi-Corp have come to a new conclusion after all the events that've gone down. While they can't make medi-porters available to <i>every</i> citizen, Medi-Corp is starting a program where they'll give out medi-porters to the handicapped and elderly of Paragon City. Their reasoning is that these are the people who need them the most, given that if they're in a life threatening situation, these folks won't be able to get themselves to a hospital. While the folks who were pushing for the widespread handout of the tech still aren't fully happy, they've at least got something, huh?<br><br>Finally, the boys at Medi-Corp have finished implementing the new tech. About time, huh? You would think they'd need it to get lost a few more times before gettin' it right. This means you hero folks are gonna be a-OK when you're going up against Cole's big bad Praetorians. As for me? Well, I've still got some business here on behalf of the FBSA, like helpin' out Harken's family. They're pretty broken up about his death, and I don't blame 'em. He might've started this whole situation, but all the man wanted was to do some good. It's the fault of groups like Malta and the Sky Raiders that folks ended up dying today. <br><br>Anyway, I'm sure you've got plenty of other issues to handle, and I've got a wife who is gonna kill me if I don't make it home for dinner at least once this week."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2494697663" "Well, okay, we're not <i>exactly</i> going to give them the technology. I've got a plan. I'm going to have the schematics of the base we're probably going to sent to my PDA. That's right, {HeroName}, old Roy is tagging along for this one. We're going to make this a two prong operation.<br><br>On your end, you'll be handling 'giving' them the tech and tracking down this Peter fellow to put a stop to the Sky Raider operation and Malta's involvement in it. On my end, I'll be working on recovering the president and the tech. If I know the Raiders, they'll have you transfer the data on the tech through a computer. I'll hack into the computer and finish the backup process that Medi-Corp was doing. When it's done, I'll fry the copy that the Sky Raiders have and rescue Zanella.<br><br>You've got the hard part. You'll have to fight through the entire Sky Raider base and get to this 'Peter' person. Make sure you bring him in, along with any Sky Raiders working with him."
// AcceptString :
"P2072388116" "Sounds good. Anything else?"
// SendOffString :
"P2136670923" "Aside from being <color orange>very careful because you'll be going into an extremely dangerous situation?</color> There is one other thing. <color yellow>If you've worked before with agent Jenni Adair from SAM, you can contact her subordinate, Keith Nance, and request his help in this operation before going in. </color> That's everything I can think of. I'll see you on the other side, {HeroName}. Let's hope neither of us gets killed, eh?"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4224392020" "End the Medi-Port Conspiracy"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P361956274" "No time to talk, {HeroName}. We've got to keep moving."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2035459115" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: The Value of Life </color>"

